# SUNWAKE — High Tide on the Malecón

An original open-world crime game set in **Port Alcira**, a sun-soaked Latin-Caribbean coastal city.
Juno Reyes comes home after six years to find developer **Augusto Brandt** and his muscle, **Los Gaviotas**,
buying up the neighbourhood one roof at a time. Steal cars, outrun the **APD**, and take the Malecón back.

It runs in desktop Chrome from plain static files (three.js r160 vendored), with no build step and no network
requests. The city, the people, the cars, the music and every sound are generated in code.

![cover](screenshots/1-chase.jpg)

## In numbers

**12 story missions** in 3 acts · **38 activities** · **32 vehicles** · **11 weapons** · **9 districts** with
**18 named places** · **6 radio stations** · a crew of 3 with health bars · 3 save slots. The numbers come from
`game/src/core/catalog.js`, which counts the content tables, and the pause map shows them as big tiles.

| Activities (38) | |
|---|---|
| 4 street races | Malecón Sprint, Lantana Loop, Docks Dash, Mirador Climb |
| 6 properties | Casa Mirador, Odalys Stake, Club Marea, Boathouse 9, Cine Farol, Penthouse Alta |
| 4 stunt jumps | ramps across the grid with airtime bonuses |
| 8 taxi fares | Night Owl, Hotel Hop, Banker's Lunch, Last Showing, Shift Change, Lighthouse Date, Checkout, On Air |
| 6 deliveries | Taco Run, Parts Run, Fresh Catch, Cement Mixer, Scrap Metal, Lamp Oil (timed, with tips) |
| 4 strangers & side stories | Don Elio's *The Keeper's Lamp*, Doña Pilar's *Abuela's Records*, Kiko's *The Runaway Parrot*, Chef Amparo's *Wedding Cake* |
| 5 bounties | "El Cangrejo" Ruiz, Dora "La Grúa" Paz, Teo "Salitre" Vega, Lupe "Navaja" Soto, Bruno "Faro" Ibarra |
| 1 collectible set | 20 pieces of sea glass |

Vehicles (32): Caldera GT, Rayo Coupé, Trueno Muscle, Alba Coupé, Paloma Cabrio, Solano Sedan, Mérida Luxe,
Marquesa Limo, Brisa Wagon, Gaviota SUV, Vespa Kite, Mango Taxi, Tarpón Pickup, Mula 4x4 (lifted), Grúa Tow
Truck, Toro Van, Pelícano Cargo, Nieve Ice-Cream Van, Reposo Hearse, Luz Ambulance, Bombero Pumper, Basura
Hauler, Flete Box Truck, Coral Bus, Ibis Bike, Chispa Scooter, APD Interceptor, APD Ranger, APD Moto; and three
boats: Marlin speedboats at the pier, Cayo skiffs and the Sirena yacht at Isla Faro.

Weapons (11): fists, Corta machete, Vesper 9, Mako SMG, Breaker 12, Kestrel AR, Marlin DMR, Garza sniper,
Bengala flare gun (sets cars alight), Trueno grenade launcher, Tormenta rocket launcher.

## Features

- **A whole city**: a 10×10-block grid in nine districts (Palm Heights, Mirador Hills, Ciudad Alta, Marea Beach,
  Old Quay, Barrio Coral, Little Lantana, Ferro Docks and Isla Faro), towers with setbacks and rooftop tanks,
  pastel beach hotels with balconies, villas with hip roofs, shops with awnings, warehouses and container stacks,
  palm boulevards, street lights, neon strips in Barrio Coral and Little Lantana, a beach with umbrellas, a pier
  with a marina, and **Isla Faro**: a lighthouse island with a turning beam, a cantina and a jetty, reached by a
  stone causeway from the sand.
- **Day and night**: a gradient sky with a moving sun, long golden-hour shadows, lit windows, lamps and neon at night.
- **On foot and by car**: third-person walking, sprinting, jumping and over-the-shoulder aiming; 29 drivable
  original vehicles (sports and muscle cars, coupes, a cabrio, sedans, a limo, a hearse, wagons and SUVs, a taxi,
  pickups and a lifted 4x4, a tow truck with a boom, vans, an ice-cream van with a cone on the roof, an ambulance,
  a fire pumper with a ladder, a garbage hauler, a box truck, a city bus, a motorbike with a rider who leans into
  turns, a step-through scooter, and the APD fleet) with arcade handling, handbrake drifts, jumps, damage, smoke,
  fire and explosions; enter, exit and carjack with **F**.
- **Living streets**: 30 traffic vehicles drawn from 26 civilian models that follow lanes, turn at junctions and
  brake; 46 sidewalk pedestrians plus
  a crowd of 22 on the Malecón promenade and the beach; people run from gunfire, crashes and chases, and some
  freeze and duck with their hands over their heads.
- **Five-star APD**: crimes raise the wanted level; Interceptors, Ranger SUVs and Moto units with callsigns respond, pursue, ram, and drop officers
  who shoot; the AIR-1 helicopter with a spotlight from 3★, roadblocks from 4★, line of sight, a search zone and
  a cool-down. A live dispatch panel lists every unit and its status. Get caught on foot at low heat and you are
  BUSTED; die and you are WASTED and wake up at Clínica Luz.
- **Combat**: 11 weapon slots (fists, Vesper 9, Mako SMG, Breaker 12, Kestrel AR, Marlin DMR, Tormenta launcher,
  Corta machete, Bengala flare gun, Garza sniper, Trueno grenade launcher) with ammo, locked slots with prices, hitscan with tracers, muzzle flashes, sparks and explosions; red markers
  over armed enemies; an on-foot weapon panel with a big ammo count.
- **Story**: 12 jobs in three acts for Odalys, Pike, Nix, Marisol and Tío Benny, each with 3-5 stages: talk, steal,
  steal a marked car, timed drives, gunfights, chases, escapes. Rewards, REP and weapon unlocks.
- **Activities**: 4 street races with rivals and checkpoints, 6 properties with daily income (each one you own
  is a safehouse where you can save), 8 taxi fares and 6 deliveries against the clock, 4 strangers & side stories
  (a named local on the sidewalk asks a favour, on foot or by car), 5 bounty hunts, 20 sea-glass collectibles,
  4 stunt jumps, the Ferretería gun shop and the Clínica.
- **Pike Customs**: a garage with your car on a turntable, stat bars and upgrades (engine, brakes, armour,
  bulletproof tyres, respray, repair) with prices and levels.
- **Crew of three**: **Z** Pike swaps the plates (drops a star), **X** Marisol leaves a tuned getaway car at the
  kerb, **C** Nix opens the scanner (every APD unit on the radar); a HUD strip shows their portraits, names,
  hotkeys and cooldowns. Calling the crew under heat costs them health (8 per star); a member below 25 is laid
  up until they recover past 40.
- **AIR-1**: a thin, crisp searchlight beam and a bright lit ellipse that follows you on the road.
- **HUD**: mission card with stage bar, timer and kill counter, APD dispatch, cash, clock, stars, rank and REP,
  weapon slots, crew strip, district standing, a rotating round minimap with GPS route and search circle,
  health/armour, dialogue with drawn portraits, speedometer and gear, radio station and song.
- **Map screen as a career dashboard** (**M**): seven big count tiles (missions, activities, vehicles, weapons,
  districts, radio, % complete), the district map with all 18 named places and Isla Faro, typed blips with a
  legend and the GPS route (click to set a waypoint), the story by act with ticks and locks, a % complete ring,
  the crew with portraits, health bars and ability status, per-activity progress, and the three save slots, all
  on one screen.
- **Menus and saves**: a title screen over the live city, three save slots with progress, autosave after every
  job, a pause menu with map, story, stats, save and controls tabs.
- **Sound**: a Web Audio synth for the engine, sirens, guns, crashes and explosions, and six procedural radio
  stations, each with its own tempo, key, scale, chord progression, voices and drum pattern: Ola FM 97.3 (beach
  pop), Radio Farol 101.5 (bolero), Bassline 88.8 (club), Salsa Brava 94.1 (salsa), Cumbia Coral 90.7 (cumbia),
  Noche Synth 106.6 (synthwave).

## Controls

| On foot | | Driving | |
|---|---|---|---|
| W A S D | move | W / S | throttle / brake, reverse |
| Shift / Space | sprint / jump | A / D | steer |
| Mouse (click to lock) | look | Space | handbrake |
| Right / left mouse | aim / shoot | Q | radio station |
| 1-9, 0, wheel | weapons | F | get out (bail at speed) |
| | | Left mouse | drive-by shooting |
| F | enter or steal a car | Z / X / C | crew abilities |
| E / R | use shop, buy / ammo | M, Esc | map, pause |

## Run it

```sh
node serve.ts          # serves game/ on http://localhost:8080
```

Then open http://localhost:8080 in desktop Chrome and click NEW GAME.

## Layout

```
game/index.html, style.css     HUD / menu markup and styles
game/src/main.js               renderer, game states, frame loop, car enter/exit, actor collisions
game/src/core/                 config (all names), catalog (content counts), input, audio synth, save slots, random
game/src/world/                city (grid, buildings, props, queries), sky (day/night), marina, geometry helpers
game/src/actors/               player, person, vehicle, traffic, peds, police, gang, crew
game/src/combat/weapons.js     weapon table, hitscan, crimes
game/src/fx/effects.js         tracers, explosions, fire, smoke, markers, speed streaks
game/src/missions/             storyData (12 jobs), story runner, activities, races, properties, side jobs + bounties
game/src/ui/                   hud, minimap, menus, garage
game/src/shots.js              the screenshot scenes (real game states)
game/src/tests/playtest.js     scripted playtest through the game loop
tools/shoot.mjs                headless-Chrome screenshots and playtest (Node, no dependencies)
```

`node tools/shoot.mjs all` renders the screenshots; `node tools/shoot.mjs playtest` runs the playtest.

